<title>FRANCE: France denies new CL recovery plan letter.</title>
<headline>France denies new CL recovery plan letter.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French finance ministry denied on Thursday a newspaper report that it had submitted a new recovery plan in a letter to the European Commission.</p>
<p>&quot;We have not sent a letter on a new rescue plan,&quot; a finance ministry official said.</p>
<p>In Brussels, the European Commission also denied the report in French daily La Tribune Desfosses that it had received a letter outlining plans to soften the terms of last year's state rescue of state bank Credit Lyonnais.</p>
</text>
